{
  "version": 2,
  "description": "Shared explicit-source normalization contract. The first valid candidate wins; callers determine source precedence. Client-side 5B persistence remains out of scope. Raw HTTP Accept-Language uses a strict bounded language-range profile with q-sorting; these raw-header cases are not standalone-tag fixtures. Standalone boundary trimming accepts U+0020, U+0009, U+000A, U+000D and U+000B only; NUL is rejected before trimming.",
